DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, 0, 6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 6, -3, 6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, 0, 6>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, -3, 6>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-6, 0, 6>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, 0, 6>") x Compute("<6, -3, 6>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, -3, 6>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, 0, 6>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 4, -5, -4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 10, 9, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -1, 1, -10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, -5, -4>") x Compute("<-1, 1, -10>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<10, 9, 10>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<4, -5, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, 9, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -8, -4, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, -5, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 4, 6, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<5, -5, -3>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, -5, -3>") . Compute("<4, 6, 10>")}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, 6, 10>") . Compute("<5, -5, -3>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, -5, -3>") x Compute("<4, 6, 10>")}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, 6, 10>") . Compute("<-8, -4, 2>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, -5, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
